# Build context exclusions for docker/server.Dockerfile. BuildKit reads
# <Dockerfile>.dockerignore next to the Dockerfile in preference to a
# .dockerignore at the context root, so this applies to `docker build -f
# docker/server.Dockerfile .` and to the compose build.
.git
.github
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.log
# Settings with secrets, anywhere in the tree (a checkout's .env holds the
# master key), and local state that is not source: backups hold the
# database, and the worktrees and the pnpm store are large.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
backups/
.worktrees/
.pnpm-store/
**/.DS_Store
# Packaged desktop releases are not server inputs.
apps/desktop/release
# The self-hosted images are labelled Apache-2.0, so code under another
# license stays out of them: ee/ is proprietary (ee/LICENSE) and the mobile
# app reserves all rights (apps/mobile/LICENSE). Nothing these images build
# depends on either, and pnpm's frozen install accepts the missing projects.
ee/
apps/mobile/
